Subject: [PATCH] fritchii-tablecharge: pointer table entries are charged only for bindings the first pass left free.

fritchii-tablecharge: pointer table entries are charged only for bindings the first pass left free.
Switch EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_TABLECHARGE=1, off by default (Common::PeSwitch).

Upstream: Frizti/Fritchii a0bcae9b25 "shader: charge pointer table entries only for bindings the
first pass left free" (cherry-pick of 4ff805a0c0), from zortos293/Lichii#421, also the first commit
of #434; merged as b727011f95 into fritchii-v4 ("Hyrule Field grass no longer disappears").

What it fixes: GlobalMemoryToStorageBufferPass binds pointer table entries in the storage buffer
bindings the pass without them leaves free (table_budget). The second pass started from an empty
set, so a table entry's holder that the first pass had bound (and so already kept out of the
budget) was charged again and shut out other tables. Ocarina's foliage culling compute
331e607152ce78d5 bound 28 of 32 bindings and 4 of its 8 per-type instance tables; a plant type
whose table is not bound is culled whole. Upstream: all 8 tables with the fix (541ba22d44898196: 7,
was 6).

With the switch: the second pass carries the first pass's set as `counted`; candidates and holders
in it take nothing from table_budget. If the result plus the reserved NVN bindings still goes past
the stage limit, the program keeps the first pass's buffers (tables left out, bindings_full, so the
"All N storage buffer bindings taken" warning still shows). Unset: `counted` stays empty, the
takes_binding test is the old test, and the second pass is the old code path (moves included).

Deviations from upstream:
- Switch-gated (upstream is unconditional).
- Our stage limit is StorageBufferLimit(env) (0350 EDEN_UP_WIDE_COMPUTE_SSBOS) minus our T61
  PendingNvnBindings reservation, so the fallback compares set.size() + reserved with the limit.
- The fallback sets bindings_full (upstream drops silently) so the PS5 log still says it happened.
- Catch2 tests not ported (no test build here).

PS5: logs from 6-9 Nov show "All 32 storage buffer bindings taken, the rest stay global" about 5
times per run in Kokiri (2012 lines in 411 logs). Test together with EDEN_UP_WIDE_COMPUTE_SSBOS=1
(Fritchii needs 33 bindings in Hyrule Field, 37 in Castle Town) and, for task/mesh grass programs,
fritchii-gfx64ssbo (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_GFX64SSBO=1). Programs whose bindings change get new SPIR-V and miss the driver pipeline cache once.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp
index 61f8397..cb447e4 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/global_memory_to_storage_buffer_pass.cpp
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@ struct StorageInfo {
     size_t table_budget{};
     size_t table_used{};
     small_vector<StorageBufferAddr, 8> table_candidates;
+    /// The storage buffers the pass without table entries bound. Bound again, they take nothing
+    /// from table_budget, which they were already left out of (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_TABLECHARGE).
+    /// Empty without the switch.
+    StorageBufferSet counted;
     /// A buffer was left out, its accesses global: every binding was taken.
     bool bindings_full{};
 };
@@ -1416,10 +1420,15 @@ void CollectStorageBuffers(IR::Block& block, IR::Inst& inst, StorageInfo& info,
             for (const StorageBufferAddr& candidate : candidates) {
                 const StorageBufferAddr holder{.index = candidate.index,
                                                .offset = candidate.offset};
+                // A buffer takes a binding unless this pass or the one before it (counted) bound
+                // it; counted is empty without EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_TABLECHARGE.
+                const auto takes_binding = [&info](const StorageBufferAddr& buffer) {
+                    return info.set.find(buffer) == info.set.end() &&
+                           !info.counted.contains(buffer);
+                };
                 const size_t added{
-                    (info.set.find(candidate) == info.set.end() ? 1U : 0U) +
-                    (candidate.indirect != ~0U && info.set.find(holder) == info.set.end() ? 1U
-                                                                                          : 0U)};
+                    (takes_binding(candidate) ? 1U : 0U) +
+                    (candidate.indirect != ~0U && takes_binding(holder) ? 1U : 0U)};
                 const bool table{std::ranges::find(info.table_candidates, candidate) !=
                                  info.table_candidates.end()};
                 if ((table && info.table_used + added > info.table_budget) ||
@@ -1720,12 +1729,29 @@ void GlobalMemoryToStorageBufferPass(Environment& env, IR::Program& program,
     if (info.tables_seen && info.set.size() + reserved < StorageBufferLimit(env)) {
         // Again with pointer table entries, in the bindings the first pass left free.
         StorageInfo with_tables;
-        with_tables.iterator_words = std::move(info.iterator_words);
-        with_tables.atomic_pointers = std::move(info.atomic_pointers);
         with_tables.tables_enabled = true;
         with_tables.table_budget = StorageBufferLimit(env) - info.set.size() - reserved;
-        info = std::move(with_tables);
-        collect();
+        // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_TABLECHARGE=1 (zortos293/Lichii#421, Fritchii a0bcae9b25): the buffers
+        // the first pass bound take nothing from table_budget when this pass binds them again,
+        // and a result past the stage limit falls back to the first pass's buffers.
+        static const bool charge_once = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_TABLECHARGE");
+        if (charge_once) {
+            with_tables.iterator_words = info.iterator_words;
+            with_tables.atomic_pointers = info.atomic_pointers;
+            with_tables.counted = info.set;
+            std::swap(info, with_tables);
+            collect();
+            if (info.set.size() + reserved > StorageBufferLimit(env)) {
+                // Never more storage buffers than a stage binds: without the table entries, then.
+                info = std::move(with_tables);
+                info.bindings_full = true;
+            }
+        } else {
+            with_tables.iterator_words = std::move(info.iterator_words);
+            with_tables.atomic_pointers = std::move(info.atomic_pointers);
+            info = std::move(with_tables);
+            collect();
+        }
     } else if (info.tables_seen) {
         info.bindings_full = true;
     }
